#!/usr/bin/python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# Parcha Nearby (ticket #149): send files to nearby computers and phones, and receive them,
# over the local network, with no account and no internet.
#
#   parchaos-nearby [FILE...]   the window: nearby devices, click one to send the files
#   parchaos-nearby --service   the part that stays running for the session (a systemd --user
#                               service) so others can find this computer and send to it
#
# It speaks the LocalSend protocol v2 (https://github.com/localsend/protocol), so it works
# with the LocalSend apps for phones and other computers, and with other ParchaOS computers.
# This is our own implementation, written from the protocol description:
#   - discovery: a JSON announcement to the multicast group 224.0.0.167, port 53317; others
#     answer with POST /api/localsend/v2/register (or a multicast reply). When nothing answers,
#     the local network is asked address by address, as the protocol suggests.
#   - sending: POST /prepare-upload with the file list; the receiver decides; then one
#     POST /upload per accepted file.
#   - HTTPS with a self-signed certificate made on first use; a device is known by the SHA-256
#     of its certificate (its fingerprint), which is checked before anything is sent to it.
#
# Receiving always asks first (a notification with Accept and Decline, also shown in the
# window); accepted files go to Downloads. "Let nearby devices send me files" turns it off.
#
# Original code for ParchaOS, GPL-3.0-or-later.

